        ("ku", "cap3") => "دروستکردنی سێوی مێخەک بە شێوەی هاوبەش",
        ("ku", "cap4") => "سێوی مێخەک‌ڕێژ بە شێوەی جیاواز",
        ("ku", "cap5") => "پێشکەشکردنی دیاریی سێوی مێخەک‌ڕێژ",

        ("en", "title") => "Sêva Mîxekrêj · the Kurdish clove apple",
        ("en", "kicker") => "KURDISH CULTURAL HERITAGE",
        ("en", "back") => "Back to home",
        ("en", "heroAlt") => "A woman decorating an apple with cloves",
        ("en", "intro") => "Sêva Mîxekrêj, the clove-studded apple, is a handmade keepsake associated in some Kurdish communities with love, longing, devotion and memory.",
        ("en", "paragraph1") => "The clove apple is a striking example of material culture and emotional symbolism in some Kurdish communities. Made from a simple apple and whole cloves, it can carry stories of love, longing, affection and remembrance.",
        ("en", "paragraph2") => "A firm, attractive apple is chosen and carefully studded with cloves. The time and attention devoted to making it are part of the gift's meaning: its value lies not only in its appearance, but also in the feeling behind its making.",
        ("en", "paragraph3") => "In some oral accounts, the clove apple was exchanged between people in love and could express affection, longing, waiting or reconciliation. It can be understood as a quiet language of feeling.",
        ("en", "paragraph4") => "Its keeping qualities also contribute to its meaning. Cloves can affect how an apple dries and help retain its scent, but how long it lasts as a keepsake depends on how it is made and stored.",
        ("en", "paragraph5") => "Today, alongside romantic meanings, the clove apple appears in some cultural and artistic activities as a symbol of remembrance, peace and keeping memory alive. It brings together nature, handcraft, human feeling and cultural memory.",
